sunxi_a133: the GPU module can be loaded again after it was unloaded

pvr_drm_unload disables runtime PM, and sunxi_platform_term, called later in the same unload,
disabled it again. Disables are counted and a load enables it once, so after `rmmod pvrsrvkm`
every later load failed to power the GPU domain (pm_runtime_get_sync: -13) and the GPU was gone
until a reboot. The teardown now disables runtime PM only if it is still enabled. 2026-10-23.

--- a/services/system/rogue/sunxi_a133/sunxi_platform.c
+++ b/services/system/rogue/sunxi_a133/sunxi_platform.c
@@ -915,7 +915,11 @@ void sunxi_platform_term(void)
 	clk_disable_unprepare(sunxi_data->clks.bus);
 	reset_control_assert(sunxi_data->clks.reset);
 
-	pm_runtime_disable(sunxi_data->dev);
+	/* At unload pvr_drm_unload has already disabled runtime PM. Disables are counted, so a second
+	 * one would leave it disabled after the next load's one enable, and that load's
+	 * pm_runtime_get_sync() would fail with -EACCES (no GPU until a reboot). */
+	if (pm_runtime_enabled(sunxi_data->dev))
+		pm_runtime_disable(sunxi_data->dev);
 	if (sunxi_data->power_on) {
 		pm_runtime_put_noidle(sunxi_data->dev);
 		sunxi_data->power_on = 0;
